      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.045,
            0.362,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.087,
            0.856,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": "5. Identify which of the following expressions are equal to the given expression without computation. You may rewrite the expressions using terms or removing brackets. There can be more than one expression which is equal to the given expression."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.167,
            0.382,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": "(a) 83 – 37 – 12"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.191,
            0.449,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": "(i) 84 – 38 – 12"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.215,
            0.461,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": "(ii) 84 – (37 + 12)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.238,
            0.449,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "(iii) 83 – 38 – 13"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.263,
            0.459,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": "(iv) – 37 + 83 –12"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.287,
            0.43,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "(b) 93 + 37 × 44 + 76"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.311,
            0.495,
            0.332
          ],
          "content": "(i) 37 + 93 × 44 + 76"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.335,
            0.496,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": "(ii) 93 + 37 × 76 + 44"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.359,
            0.523,
            0.38
          ],
          "content": "(iii) (93 + 37) × (44 + 76)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.383,
            0.496,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": "(iv) 37 × 44 + 93 + 76"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.408,
            0.855,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": "6.\t Choose a number and create ten different expressions having that value."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.413,
            0.495,
            0.599,
            0.52
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "SUMMARY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.529,
            0.831,
            0.586
          ],
          "content": "We have been reading and evaluating simple expressions for quite some time now. Here we started by revising the meaning of some simple expressions and their values."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.587,
            0.831,
            0.624
          ],
          "content": "We learnt how to compare certain expressions through reasoning instead of bluntly evaluating them."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.625,
            0.83,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": "To help read and evaluate complex expressions without confusion, we use terms and brackets."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.663,
            0.832,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": "When an expression is written as a sum of terms, changing the order of the terms or grouping the terms does not change the value of the expression. This is because the “commutative property of addition” and the “associative property of addition”, respectively."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.74,
            0.831,
            0.797
          ],
          "content": "To evaluate expressions within brackets, we saw that when we remove brackets preceded by a negative sign, the terms within the bracket change their sign."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.797,
            0.832,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": "We also learnt about the “distributive property” — multiplying a number with an expression inside brackets is equal to the multiplying the number with each term in the bracket."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.938,
            0.189,
            0.954
          ],
          "content": "44"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
